UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>Design has the power to shape our understanding of the world and our experience within it. Our Bachelor of Design will equip you with design skills in typography, branding, image-making technologies and more. Make your degree custom-fit by choosing a specialised major to develop future-focused skills. Emerge industry-ready to kick-start your career.</p> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-design/handbook"> Check the Bachelor of Design course handbook </a> <p> <a href="/courses/find-a-course/download-course-guide"> Get a copy of our course guide </a> </p> <h5> Swinburne Open Day 2026 </h5> <p>Stop by our Hawthorn campus on Sunday 26 July for Open Day – the stop where everything starts. Got everything you need? <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/courses/intakes/mid-year/">Apply for midyear now and get on your way in Semester 2</a>.</p> <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/openday/?siid=bnr_alt%7Ccamp_mid%7Csrcnam_cs%7Csrcloc_alt%7C454"> Register for Open Day </a> <h5>Available majors</h5> <ul><li> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-design/communication-design"> Communication Design </a> </li> <li> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-design/emerging-technology-for-design-innovation"> Emerging Technology for Digital Innovation </a> </li> <li> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-design/branded-environments"> Experiential Design </a> </li> <li> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-design/motion-design"> Motion Design </a> </li> <li> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-design/photomedia"> Photography </a> </li> <li> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-design/ux-interaction-design"> UX Interaction Design </a> </li> </ul> <h5>Your industry experience</h5> <p>Bolster your CV with real industry experience while you study through our Work Integrated Learning programs – a guaranteed part of all our bachelor degrees. This can include placements, internships or industry-linked projects. </p> <p>This degree includes a capstone project which could see you working with places like City of Melbourne, and more.</p> <a href="/life-at-swinburne/work-integrated-learning"> Learn more Work Integrated Learning </a> <h5>Skills you’ll learn</h5> <ul><li> Creative visual problem solving </li> <li> Design strategy </li> <li> Concept development </li> <li> Digital design skills </li> <li> Prototyping skills </li> </ul> <h5>Your career opportunities</h5> <ul><li> Graphic communication designer </li> <li> Motion graphics designer </li> <li> Photographer / videographer </li> <li> User experience designer </li> <li> Web and app designer </li> <li> Exhibition, retail space and set designer </li> </ul> <h5>Key codes</h5> <p> CRICOS course code </p> <p> 088395D </p> <p> VTAC Code (IFP) </p> <p> 3400210713 </p> <h5> International student visa </h5> <p>International students in Australia who hold student visas are required to study full-time and on campus. Courses that are taught entirely online are only available to international students studying outside Australia or those in Australia who are not on a student visa. Online courses are not available to international students in Australia who hold a student visa.</p> <h5>Why Swinburne?</h5> <p>Ranked Top 150 in Art and Design</p> <p>QS World University Rankings by Subject 2023</p> <p>5 stars for overall experience</p> <p>#1 in Melbourne for graduate found full-time employment 4 months after completing their degree </p> <p>#1 in Melbourne for graduate salary one year out</p> <p><a href="/life-at-swinburne/why-choose-swinburne/sources">Sources</a></p> <h5>Double degrees</h5> <p>Combine your design degree with a second degree to gain diverse skills, expand your career pathays, and graduate with two qualifications. Here are some options:</p> <ul><li> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-design-bachelor-of-media-and-communication/"> Design/Media and Communication </a> </li> <li> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-design-bachelor-of-business/"> Design/Business </a> </li> <li> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-design-bachelor-of-applied-innovation/"> Design/Applied Innovation </a> </li> </ul> <p> <a href="#"> Close video </a> </p> <p>Michael''s Next Gen Story</p> <h5> Michael''s Next Gen_ Story </h5> <p>It’s this piece of paper – a Swinburne Bachelor of Design Communications - that has enabled Michael to successfully kick off his career. Now working at a Melbourne advertising agency, a Swinburne degree gives graduates, like Michael, real industry experience to prepare them for the workforce. Michael got more than a piece of paper.</p> <p> <a href="https://commons.swinburne.edu.au/file/1d109c0e-6b94-46fe-8328-60d8b373631a/1/michael_next_gen_transcript.pdf"> View transcript [PDF 171KB] </a> </p> <p> <a href="https://www.instagram.com/soda_swinburne/"> School of Design and Architecture''s Instagram </a> </p> <h5>Related courses</h5> <ul><li> <h5> Bachelor of Design (Architecture) </h5> <p> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-design-architecture"> Discover more (Bachelor of Design (Architecture)) </a> </p> </li> <li> <h5> Diploma of Design (UniLink) </h5> <p> <a href="/course/degree-pathway/diploma-of-design-unilink-dp-des1"> Discover more (Diploma of Design (UniLink)) </a> </p> </li> <li> <h5> Advanced Diploma of Screen and Media - Film and Television </h5> <p> <a href="/course/tafe/advanced-diploma-of-screen-and-media-film-and-television"> Discover more (Advanced Diploma of Screen and Media - Film and Television) </a> </p> </li> </ul>',
