UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>Flourish into a skilled, innovative and compassionate healthcare professional with the Bachelor of Nursing. You’ll gain clinical competence and leadership skills through a balance of real-world learning, simulation labs and the latest digital health technology. </p> <p>Through deep industry partnerships, you’ll complete over 800 hours of supervised placement and gain extensive experience in hospitals, community health, aged care and mental health settings.</p> <p>Please note: due to high interest and limited capacity, students are encouraged to apply early to secure a place within this course. This course is available in Swinburne''s Hawthorn and Wantirna campuses.</p> <p> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-nursing/handbook"> Check the Bachelor of Nursing course handbook </a> </p> <p> <a href="/courses/find-a-course/download-course-guide"> Get a copy of our course guide </a> </p> <h5> Swinburne Open Day 2026 </h5> <p>Stop by our Hawthorn campus on Sunday 26 July for Open Day – the stop where everything starts. Got everything you need? <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/courses/intakes/mid-year/">Apply for midyear now and get on your way in Semester 2</a>.</p> <p> <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/openday/?siid=bnr_alt%7Ccamp_mid%7Csrcnam_cs%7Csrcloc_alt%7C454"> Register for Open Day </a> </p> <h5>Your industry experience</h5> <p>All our bachelor degrees include a guaranteed Work Integrated Learning opportunity. This degree features work placement as a professional accreditation requirement. You’ll complete 800 clinical practicum hours in varied clinical settings. In Nursing Projects (NUR30007), you''ll collaborate with industry partners on a student-led project. </p> <p> <a href="/life-at-swinburne/work-integrated-learning"> Explore Work Integrated Learning </a> </p> <h5>Skills you’ll learn</h5> <ul><li> Critical thinking </li> <li> Flexibility and adaptability </li> <li> Problem solving skills </li> <li> Patient safety and well-being </li> <li> Wound management </li> <li> Communication </li> </ul> <h5>Your career opportunities</h5> <ul><li> Registered nurse (RN) </li> <li> Acute and Critical Care Nurse </li> <li> Community and Primary Health Nurse </li> <li> Aged Care Nurse </li> <li> Mental Health Nurse </li> <li> Health Promotion or Research Nurse </li> <li> Leadership or academic careers in health and nursing education </li> </ul> <h5>Key codes</h5> <p> CRICOS course code </p> <p> 097923K </p> <p> VTAC Code (IFP) </p> <p> 3400211303 </p> <h5> International student visa </h5> <p>International students in Australia who hold student visas are required to study full-time and on campus. Courses that are taught entirely online are only available to international students studying outside Australia or those in Australia who are not on a student visa. Online courses are not available to international students in Australia who hold a student visa.</p> <h5>Location options</h5> <ul><li> <a href="/life-at-swinburne/locations/hawthorn-campus"> Hawthorn </a> </li> </ul> <h5>Professional accreditations</h5> <ul><li> <a href="https://www.nursingmidwiferyboard.gov.au/"> <h5> Nursing and Midwifery Board of Australia </h5> </a> </li> <li> <a href="https://www.ahpra.gov.au/"> <h5> Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency </h5> </a> </li> </ul> <ul><li> <p>"My experience at the Royal Women’s Hospital was nothing short of amazing. It''s difficult to articulate how much gratitude I have for the staff, who went to great lengths to make sure us students felt supported and empowered."</p> <p> Rachael , Bachelor of Nursing </p> </li> </ul> <h5>Why Swinburne?</h5> <p>5 stars for learner engagement</p> <p>1# in Melbourne for staff: student interaction</p> <p>#1 in Melbourne for graduate satisfaction</p> <p>93% of graduates found employment within 4 months of completing their course</p> <p><a href="/life-at-swinburne/why-choose-swinburne/sources">Sources</a><br/></p> <h5>Related courses</h5> <ul><li> <h5> Diploma of Nursing </h5> <p> <a href="/course/tafe/diploma-of-nursing"> Discover more (Diploma of Nursing) </a> </p> </li> <li> <h5> Bachelor of Health Science </h5> <p> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-health-science"> Discover more (Bachelor of Health Science) </a> </p> </li> <li> <h5> Diploma of Health Science (UniLink) </h5> <p> <a href="/course/degree-pathway/diploma-of-health-science-unilink-dp-hsc1"> Discover more (Diploma of Health Science (UniLink)) </a> </p> </li> </ul>',
