    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4><h5>Qualifications</h5> <p>You must have completed a three-year degree with a minimum average of 65% in the final year units of study. Other relevant experience will also be taken into account in assessing your application.<br/></p> <h5> Admission requirements </h5> <p>Meeting the minimum entry requirements for the course does not guarantee an offer of a place. <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/courses/applying/how-to-apply-research-degree/entry-requirements/">Check admission requirements</a> for general information about the admission process.</p> <h5>English language requirements</h5> <p>Satisfactory completion of one of the following:</p> <ul><li>IELTS overall band of 6.5 (Academic Module) with no individual band below 6.0</li> <li>Swinburne’s <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/study/international/apply/entry-requirements/">English for Academic Purposes</a> (EAP 5 Advanced level) with overall 70%, all skills 65% or above</li> <li>or equivalent measures available at <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/study/international/apply/entry-requirements/">English language requirements</a>.</li> </ul> <h5> Need to undertake an English assessment for entry? </h5> <p>A prerequisite for many courses, the Pearson Test of English (PTE Academic) can now be done at our Hawthorn campus.</p> <p> <a href="/courses/planning-your-future/admission-requirements/pearson-test-english"> Book your Pearson Test of English </a> </p> <h5>Finding your fit</h5> <p>At Swinburne, we recognise that not one size fits all. If this course doesn’t meet all your study criteria, check out these alternatives.</p> <ul><li> <h5> Master of Business (Research) </h5> <p> <a href="/course/research/master-of-business-research"> Discover more (Master of Business (Research)) </a> </p> </li> <li> <h5> Master of Research (Design) </h5> <p> <a href="/course/research/master-of-research-design"> Discover more (Master of Research (Design)) </a> </p> </li> <li> <h5> Master of Research (Humanities, Arts and Social Sciences) </h5> <p> <a href="/course/research/master-of-research-humanities-arts-and-social-sciences"> Discover more (Master of Research (Humanities, Arts and Social Sciences)) </a> </p> </li> </ul>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.swinburne.edu.au/course/research/master-of-arts-research/?student_type=international',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '046751C';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>Accounting is about more than numbers. It’s about how finances affect businesses and people’s lives. Swinburne''s Bachelor of Accounting aims to develop the technical skills and personal traits you need to adapt and thrive in this rapidly evolving profession. </p> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-accounting/handbook"> Check the Bachelor of Accounting course handbook </a> <p> <a href="/courses/find-a-course/download-course-guide"> Get a copy of our course guide </a> </p> <h5> Swinburne Open Day 2026 </h5> <p>Stop by our Hawthorn campus on Sunday 26 July for Open Day – the stop where everything starts. Got everything you need? <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/courses/intakes/mid-year/">Apply for midyear now and get on your way in Semester 2</a>.</p> <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/openday/?siid=bnr_alt%7Ccamp_mid%7Csrcnam_cs%7Csrcloc_alt%7C454"> Register for Open Day </a> <h5>Available majors</h5> <ul><li> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-accounting/accounting"> Accounting </a> </li> </ul> <h5> Future-proof your accounting career </h5> <p>The world’s best businesses don’t just keep up with change – they create it. Technology is transforming every industry, and those who understand it will lead the charge. Add a minor in Computer Science, Data Analytics, FinTech, ICT or Managing Information Systems and graduate ready to drive the digital transformation, not follow it. </p> <h5>Your industry experience</h5> <p>Bolster your CV with real industry experience through our Work Integrated Learning programs, guaranteed in all our bachelor degrees. In the Industry Consulting Project (BUS30009), you''ll work on an industry partner project. Graduates find work in: commerce, public sector, financial industry, business consulting and public accounting.</p> <a href="/life-at-swinburne/work-integrated-learning"> Explore Work Integrated Learning </a> <h5>Skills you’ll learn</h5> <ul><li> Commercial awareness </li> <li> Time management </li> <li> Excel and other programs </li> <li> Problem-solving </li> <li> Ethical conduct </li> <li> Communication </li> </ul> <h5>Your career opportunities</h5> <ul><li> Public accountant </li> <li> Business consultant </li> <li> Account manager </li> <li> Analyst </li> <li> Executive officer </li> <li> Corporate accountant </li> </ul> <h5>Key codes</h5> <p> CRICOS course code </p> <p> 088381K </p> <p> VTAC Code (IFP) </p> <p> 3400210653 </p> <h5> International student visa </h5> <p>International students in Australia who hold student visas are required to study full-time and on campus. Courses that are taught entirely online are only available to international students studying outside Australia or those in Australia who are not on a student visa. Online courses are not available to international students in Australia who hold a student visa.</p> <h5>Professional accreditations</h5> <ul><li> <a href="https://www.aacsb.edu/"> <h5> AACSB Accredited </h5> </a> </li> <li> <a href="https://www.accaglobal.com/gb/en.html"> <h5> Association of Chartered Certified Accountants </h5> </a> </li> <li> <a href="https://www.cpaaustralia.com.au"> <h5> Certified Practising Accountants Australia </h5> </a> </li> <li> <a href="https://www.charteredaccountantsanz.com"> <h5> Chartered Accountants ANZ </h5> </a> </li> <li> <a href="https://www.aicpa-cima.com/home"> <h5> Chartered Institute of Management Accountants </h5> </a> </li> <li> <a href="https://www.publicaccountants.org.au/"> <h5> Institute of Public Accountants </h5> </a> </li> </ul> <h5>Why Swinburne?</h5> <p>Top 300 for business and economics</p> <p>5 stars for student support</p> <p>Top 5% of the world’s higher education business schools</p> <p>#1 in Melbourne for graduate salary one year out </p> <p><a href="/life-at-swinburne/why-choose-swinburne/sources">Sources</a></p> <h5>Double degrees</h5> <p>Combine your Accounting degree with a second degree to gain diverse skills, expand your career pathays, and graduate with two qualifications. Here are some options:</p> <ul><li> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-accounting-bachelor-of-applied-innovation"> Accounting/Applied Innovation </a> </li> </ul> <ul><li> <ul><li> Business </li> </ul> <h5> Swinburne Business School awarded AACSB International accreditation </h5> <p> AACSB International accreditation places Swinburne among the highest quality business schools in the world. </p> <p> <a href="/news/2019/07/swinburne-business-school-awarded-aacsb-international-accreditation"> Read more (Swinburne Business School awarded AACSB International accreditation) </a> </p> <p> Tuesday 30 July 2019 </p> </li> </ul> <h5>Related courses</h5> <ul><li> <h5> Bachelor of Business </h5> <p> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-business"> Discover more (Bachelor of Business) </a> </p> </li> <li> <h5> Bachelor of Business Analytics/Bachelor of Business </h5> <p> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-business-analytics-bachelor-of-business"> Discover more (Bachelor of Business Analytics/Bachelor of Business) </a> </p> </li> <li> <h5> Bachelor of Arts / Bachelor of Business </h5> <p> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-arts-bachelor-of-business"> Discover more (Bachelor of Arts / Bachelor of Business) </a> </p> </li> </ul>',
