UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>Learn effective design strategies for digital, marketing and communications collateral.</p> <p>The Bachelor of Design/Bachelor of Business equips students with the knowledge and skills essential for a career that encompasses the challenging and dynamic area of design and business. Graduates will gain opportunities in both the design and business professions learning photography, UX design and consulting skills.</p> <p> <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-design-bachelor-of-business/handbook/"> Check the Bachelor of Design / Bachelor of Business course handbook </a> </p> <p> <a href="/courses/find-a-course/download-course-guide"> Get a copy of our course guide </a> </p> <h5> Swinburne Open Day 2026 </h5> <p>Stop by our Hawthorn campus on Sunday 26 July for Open Day – the stop where everything starts. Got everything you need? <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/courses/intakes/mid-year/">Apply for midyear now and get on your way in Semester 2</a>.</p> <p> <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/openday/?siid=bnr_alt%7Ccamp_mid%7Csrcnam_cs%7Csrcloc_alt%7C454"> Register for Open Day </a> </p> <h5>Your industry experience</h5> <p>Bolster your CV with real industry experience while you study through our Work Integrated Learning programs – a guaranteed part of all our bachelor degrees. This can include placements, internships or industry-linked projects.</p> <p>This degree''s design component includes a capstone project which could see yourself working with places like City of Melbourne and more. </p> <p> <a href="/life-at-swinburne/work-integrated-learning"> Explore Work Integrated Learning </a> </p> <h5>Skills you’ll learn</h5> <ul><li> Creative visual problem solving </li> <li> Digital prototyping </li> <li> Idea generation </li> <li> Ethical conduct </li> <li> Problem solving </li> <li> Time management </li> </ul> <h5>Your career opportunities</h5> <ul><li> Economics </li> <li> Design consultancy </li> <li> Design management </li> <li> Marketing </li> <li> Merchandising </li> <li> Publishing </li> </ul> <h5>Key codes</h5> <p> CRICOS course code </p> <p> 088391G </p> <p> VTAC Code (IFP) </p> <p> 3400210723 </p> <h5> International student visa </h5> <p>International students in Australia who hold student visas are required to study full-time and on campus. Courses that are taught entirely online are only available to international students studying outside Australia or those in Australia who are not on a student visa. Online courses are not available to international students in Australia who hold a student visa.</p> <h5>Professional accreditations</h5> <ul><li> <a href="https://www.aacsb.edu/"> <h5> AACSB Accredited </h5> </a> </li> <li> <a href="https://www.unprme.org/"> <h5> PRME </h5> </a> </li> <li> <a href="https://www.accaglobal.com/gb/en.html"> <h5> Association of Chartered Certified Accountants </h5> </a> </li> <li> <a href="https://www.aicpa-cima.com/home"> <h5> Chartered Institute of Management Accountants </h5> </a> </li> <li> <a href="https://www.ahri.com.au/"> <h5> AHRI </h5> </a> </li> <li> <a href="https://www.cfainstitute.org/"> <h5> CFA Institute </h5> </a> </li> <li> <a href="https://www.aicpa-cima.com/home"> <h5> Chartered Institute of Management Accountants </h5> </a> </li> <li> <a href="https://www.cpaaustralia.com.au"> <h5> Certified Practising Accountants Australia </h5> </a> </li> <li> <a href="https://www.charteredaccountantsanz.com"> <h5> Chartered Accountants ANZ </h5> </a> </li> <li> <a href="https://www.ahri.com.au/"> <h5> AHRI </h5> </a> </li> <li> <a href="https://caia.org/"> <h5> CAIA </h5> </a> </li> </ul> <h5>Why Swinburne?</h5> <p>Ranked Top 150 in Art and Design</p> <p>QS World University Rankings by Subject 2023</p> <p>5 stars for overall experience</p> <p>Top 5% of the world’s higher education business schools</p> <p>#1 in Melbourne for graduate salary one year out</p> <p><a href="/life-at-swinburne/why-choose-swinburne/sources">Sources</a></p> <ul><li> <p>"I chose Swinburne because I wanted to complete a degree that would give me practical work experience and a competitive edge over other graduates from other universities. My placement offered insight into working life and a clearer idea of the career path I''d like to take."</p> <p> Linh , Bachelor of Design / Bachelor of Business </p> </li> </ul>',
