UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>The only thing certain about the future is that it’s uncertain. Strengthen your ability to cope with uncertainty with our Bachelor of Health Science/ Bachelor of Arts. Gain highly-transferable skills in digital literacy, analytical thinking, and communication. Examine the effects of climate change, equality, and discrimination on people''s health and wellbeing. Help people live happier, healthier lives.</p> <p> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-health-science-bachelor-of-arts/handbook"> Check the Bachelor of Health Science/ Bachelor of Arts handbook </a> </p> <p> <a href="/courses/find-a-course/download-course-guide"> Get a copy of our course guide </a> </p> <h5> Swinburne Open Day 2026 </h5> <p>Stop by our Hawthorn campus on Sunday 26 July for Open Day – the stop where everything starts. Got everything you need? <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/courses/intakes/mid-year/">Apply for midyear now and get on your way in Semester 2</a>.</p> <p> <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/openday/?siid=bnr_alt%7Ccamp_mid%7Csrcnam_cs%7Csrcloc_alt%7C454"> Register for Open Day </a> </p> <h5>Your industry experience</h5> <p>Bolster your CV with real industry experience while you study through our Work Integrated Learning programs – a guaranteed part of all our bachelor degrees. This double degree includes:</p> <ul><li>an industry-linked project</li> <li>the opportunity to apply for a career-focused placement or internship </li> <li>the chance to create real social change with industry partners in Skills and Strategies for Social Change.</li> </ul> <p> <a href="/life-at-swinburne/work-integrated-learning"> Explore Work Integrated Learning </a> </p> <h5>Skills you’ll learn</h5> <ul><li> Health science communication </li> <li> Health science research skills </li> <li> Professional and ethical behaviours </li> <li> Conceptual understanding </li> <li> Collaboration </li> <li> Critical and creative reasoning </li> </ul> <h5>Your career opportunities</h5> <ul><li> Medical researcher </li> <li> Health policy developer </li> <li> Healthcare consultant </li> <li> Community development officer </li> <li> Government relations coordinator </li> <li> Political correspondent </li> </ul> <h5>Key codes</h5> <p> CRICOS course code </p> <p> 0100752 </p> <p> VTAC Code (IFP) </p> <p> 3400211633 </p> <h5> International student visa </h5> <p>International students in Australia who hold student visas are required to study full-time and on campus. Courses that are taught entirely online are only available to international students studying outside Australia or those in Australia who are not on a student visa. Online courses are not available to international students in Australia who hold a student visa.</p> <h5>Why Swinburne?</h5> <p>Ranked Top 500 in Public Health</p> <p>ARWU Global Ranking of Academic Subjects 2022</p> <p>The only uni in Australia to have both MRI and MEG at a single site</p> <p>Top 400 for Arts and Humanities</p> <p>QS World University Rankings by Subject 2023</p> <p>5 stars for overall experience</p> <p><a href="/life-at-swinburne/why-choose-swinburne/sources">Sources</a></p> <p> <a href="#"> Close video </a> </p> <p>Bachelor of Health Science</p> <h5> Study Health Science at Swinburne </h5> <p>At Swinburne you''ll have access to cutting-edge technology, virtual reality and digital dissection tables. Combining this with real-world experience, you''ll leave more than a graduate, you''ll leave a workforce ready practitioner.</p> <p> <a href="https://commons.swinburne.edu.au/file/3fc31b2d-9b45-444d-8cdf-89c68bef3af7/1/bachelor_health_science_transcript.pdf"> Video transcript [PDF 153KB] </a> </p>',
