    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>Study network configurations, web and app programming, database design and more, and even specialise in a particular aspect of ICT-related work. Hone your knowledge in industry-class labs boasting 17 network racks and 700 Cisco devices at your disposal. Bolster your CV with work integrated learning such as placements, internships, and an industry-linked project every semester.</p> <p> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-information-and-communication-technology/handbook"> Check the Bachelor of Information and Communication Technology course handbook </a> </p> <p> <a href="/courses/find-a-course/download-course-guide"> Get a copy of our course guide </a> </p> <h5> Start in September 2026 </h5> <p>You still have time to start this degree at our Hawthorn campus. Get ahead before the year ends and reach your dream career sooner.</p> <p> <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/courses/intakes/september-intake/?siid=bnr_alt%7Ccamp_septintake%7Csrcnam_cs%7Csrcloc_alt%7C480"> Find out more </a> </p> <h5>Available majors</h5> <ul><li> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-information-and-communication-technology/information-technology"> Information Technology </a> </li> <li> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-information-and-communication-technology/network-technology"> Network Technology </a> </li> <li> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-information-and-communication-technology/software-technology"> Software Technology </a> </li> </ul> <h5> Fee-free, ATAR-free entry into this course </h5> <p>Want to study this course but don’t have an ATAR or previous study experience? Fee-Free UniReady is a free 18-week course designed to give you everything you need to study a bachelor degree at Swinburne.</p> <p> <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/courses/find-a-course/fee-free-uniready/"> Find out more </a> </p> <h5>Your industry experience</h5> <p>Build up your CV with real industry experience while you study through our Work Integrated Learning programs, which are a guaranteed part of all our bachelor degrees and can include placements, internships or industry-linked projects. In this degree, you''ll apply your learning in six professionally focused, industry-linked projects.</p> <p> <a href="/life-at-swinburne/work-integrated-learning"> Explore Work Integrated Learning </a> </p> <h5>Skills you’ll learn</h5> <ul><li> Web programming </li> <li> App programming </li> <li> Teamwork </li> <li> Server configuration </li> <li> Software maintenance </li> </ul> <h5>Your career opportunities</h5> <ul><li> Web developer </li> <li> Software designer </li> <li> Security consultant </li> <li> Mobile application developer </li> </ul> <h5>Key codes</h5> <p> CRICOS course code </p> <p> 088401M </p> <p> VTAC Code (IFP) </p> <p> 3400234173 </p> <h5> International student visa </h5> <p>International students in Australia who hold student visas are required to study full-time and on campus. Courses that are taught entirely online are only available to international students studying outside Australia or those in Australia who are not on a student visa. Online courses are not available to international students in Australia who hold a student visa.</p> <h5>Professional accreditations</h5> <ul><li> <a href="https://www.acs.org.au"> <h5> Australian Computer Society </h5> </a> </li> </ul> <h5>Why Swinburne?</h5> <p>#1 in Australia for Computer Science and Engineering</p> <p>ARWU Global Ranking of Academic Subjects 2025</p> <p>#6 in Australia for Artificial Intelligence</p> US News: Best Global Universities <p>#1 in Victoria for Graduate Employability and Salary</p> QILT Graduate Outcomes Survey (GOS) 2024 <p>Employability Category Winner for Work Integrated Learning Program</p> AFR Higher Education Awards 2024 <p><a href="/life-at-swinburne/why-choose-swinburne/sources">Sources</a></p> <h5>Double degrees</h5> <p>Combine your information and communication technology degree with a second degree to gain diverse skills, expand your career pathays, and graduate with two qualifications. Here are some options:</p> <ul><li> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-information-and-communication-technology-bachelor-of-applied-innovation/"> Information and Communication Technology/Applied Innovation </a> </li> </ul> <h5>Related courses</h5> <ul><li> <h5> Bachelor of Computer Science </h5> <p> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-computer-science"> Discover more (Bachelor of Computer Science) </a> </p> </li> <li> <h5> Diploma of Information Technology (UniLink) </h5> <p> <a href="/course/degree-pathway/diploma-of-information-technology-unilink-dp-ict1"> Discover more (Diploma of Information Technology (UniLink)) </a> </p> </li> <li> <h5> Bachelor of Cyber Security </h5> <p> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-cyber-security"> Discover more (Bachelor of Cyber Security) </a> </p> </li> </ul>',
