UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>Study network configurations, web and app programming, database design and more, and even specialise in an area of your choosing through an impressive selection of majors. Hone your knowledge in industry-class labs boasting 17 network racks and 700 Cisco devices at your disposal. Bolster your CV with full-time real industry experience, including a 12-month, paid work placement.</p> <p> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-information-and-communication-technology-professional/handbook"> Check the Bachelor of Information and Communication Technology (Professional) course handbook </a> </p> <p> <a href="/courses/find-a-course/download-course-guide"> Get a copy of our course guide </a> </p> <h5> Swinburne Open Day 2026 </h5> <p>Stop by our Hawthorn campus on Sunday 26 July for Open Day – the stop where everything starts. Got everything you need? <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/courses/intakes/mid-year/">Apply for midyear now and get on your way in Semester 2</a>.</p> <p> <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/openday/?siid=bnr_alt%7Ccamp_mid%7Csrcnam_cs%7Csrcloc_alt%7C454"> Register for Open Day </a> </p> <h5>Available majors</h5> <ul><li> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-information-and-communication-technology-professional/information-technology"> Information Technology </a> </li> <li> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-information-and-communication-technology-professional/network-technology"> Network Technology </a> </li> <li> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-information-and-communication-technology-professional/software-technology"> Software Technology </a> </li> </ul> <h5>Your industry experience</h5> <p>Build up your CV with real industry experience as you study with Work Integrated Learning, guaranteed for all our bachelor degrees. This Professional Degree includes a 12-month paid work placement and six industry-linked projects. Benefit from Swinburne’s industry partnerships, gain invaluable work experience and earn credit towards your degree. </p> <p> <a href="/life-at-swinburne/work-integrated-learning"> Explore Work Integrated Learning </a> </p> <h5>Skills you’ll learn</h5> <ul><li> Web programming </li> <li> App programming </li> <li> Teamwork </li> <li> Server configuration </li> <li> Software maintenance </li> </ul> <h5>Your career opportunities</h5> <ul><li> Web developer </li> <li> Software designer </li> <li> Security consultant </li> <li> Mobile application developer </li> </ul> <h5>Key codes</h5> <p> CRICOS </p> <p> 095881J </p> <h5> International student visa </h5> <p>International students in Australia who hold student visas are required to study full-time and on campus. Courses that are taught entirely online are only available to international students studying outside Australia or those in Australia who are not on a student visa. Online courses are not available to international students in Australia who hold a student visa.</p> <h5>Professional accreditations</h5> <ul><li> <a href="https://www.acs.org.au"> <h5> Australian Computer Society </h5> </a> </li> </ul> <h5>Why Swinburne?</h5> <p>#1 in Australia for Computer Science and Engineering</p> <p>ARWU Global Ranking of Academic Subjects 2025</p> <p>#6 in Australia for Artificial Intelligence</p> US News: Best Global Universities <p>#1 in Victoria for Graduate Employability and Salary</p> QILT Graduate Outcomes Survey (GOS) 2024 <p>Employability Category Winner for Work Integrated Learning Program</p> AFR Higher Education Awards 2024 <p><a href="/life-at-swinburne/why-choose-swinburne/sources">Sources</a></p> <h5>Related courses</h5> <ul><li> <h5> Bachelor of Information and Communication Technology </h5> <p> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-information-and-communication-technology"> Discover more (Bachelor of Information and Communication Technology) </a> </p> </li> <li> <h5> Bachelor of Arts </h5> <p> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-arts"> Discover more (Bachelor of Arts) </a> </p> </li> <li> <h5> Bachelor of Computer Science </h5> <p> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-computer-science"> Discover more (Bachelor of Computer Science) </a> </p> </li> </ul>',
