UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>Learn to disrupt, innovate and develop the fundamental skills required to help businesses and individuals with their finances. A Bachelor of Accounting and Bachelor of Applied Innovation will teach you how to master tax, auditing, economics and company law.</p> <p>Sharpen your analytical and strategic thinking skills to bring ideas to life – forecast problems that solve real-world issues and support business growth.</p> <p> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-accounting-bachelor-of-applied-innovation/handbook"> View Bachelor of Accounting / Bachelor of Applied Innovation course handbook </a> </p> <p> <a href="/courses/find-a-course/download-course-guide"> Get a copy of our course guide </a> </p> <h5> Swinburne Open Day 2026 </h5> <p>Stop by our Hawthorn campus on Sunday 26 July for Open Day – the stop where everything starts. Got everything you need? <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/courses/intakes/mid-year/">Apply for midyear now and get on your way in Semester 2</a>.</p> <p> <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/openday/?siid=bnr_alt%7Ccamp_mid%7Csrcnam_cs%7Csrcloc_alt%7C454"> Register for Open Day </a> </p> <h5>Your industry experience</h5> <p>Bolster your CV with real industry experience while you study through our Work Integrated Learning programs – a guaranteed part of all our bachelor degrees. </p> <p> <a href="/life-at-swinburne/work-integrated-learning"> Explore Work Integrated Learning </a> </p> <h5>Skills you’ll learn</h5> <ul><li> Commercial awareness </li> <li> Time management </li> <li> Excel and other programs </li> <li> Critical thinking </li> <li> Creative problem-solving </li> <li> Adaptability </li> </ul> <h5>Your career opportunities</h5> <ul><li> Public accountant </li> <li> Analyst </li> <li> Business consultant </li> <li> Innovation consultant </li> <li> Innovation analyst </li> <li> Self-employed entrepreneur </li> </ul> <h5>Key codes</h5> <p> CRICOS course code </p> <p> 108345M </p> <p> VTAC Code (IFP) </p> <p> 3400212503 </p> <h5> International student visa </h5> <p>International students in Australia who hold student visas are required to study full-time and on campus. Courses that are taught entirely online are only available to international students studying outside Australia or those in Australia who are not on a student visa. Online courses are not available to international students in Australia who hold a student visa.</p> <h5>Professional accreditations</h5> <ul><li> <a href="https://www.aacsb.edu/"> <h5> AACSB Accredited </h5> </a> </li> <li> <a href="https://www.accaglobal.com/gb/en.html"> <h5> Association of Chartered Certified Accountants </h5> </a> </li> <li> <a href="https://www.cpaaustralia.com.au"> <h5> Certified Practising Accountants Australia </h5> </a> </li> <li> <a href="https://www.charteredaccountantsanz.com"> <h5> Chartered Accountants ANZ </h5> </a> </li> <li> <a href="https://www.aicpa-cima.com/home"> <h5> Chartered Institute of Management Accountants </h5> </a> </li> <li> <a href="https://www.publicaccountants.org.au/"> <h5> Institute of Public Accountants </h5> </a> </li> </ul> <h5>Why Swinburne?</h5> <p>Top 300 for business and economics</p> <p>5 stars for student support</p> <p>Top 5% of the world’s higher education business schools</p> <p>#1 in Melbourne for graduate salary one year out </p> <p><a href="/life-at-swinburne/why-choose-swinburne/sources">Sources</a></p>',
