UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>Innovative by nature. Applied by design. Our Bachelor of Design / Bachelor of Applied Innovation double degree is tailor-made for designers who want an innovation edge. Learn in multidisciplinary innovation labs. Learn through hackathons, industry projects and innovation sprints. Get hands-on creating designs (and a page-turner of a portfolio) – from typography to digital media, to brand and identity design.</p> <p> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-design-bachelor-of-applied-innovation/handbook"> View Bachelor of Design / Bachelor of Applied Innovation course handbook </a> </p> <p> <a href="/courses/find-a-course/download-course-guide"> Get a copy of our course guide </a> </p> <h5> Swinburne Open Day 2026 </h5> <p>Stop by our Hawthorn campus on Sunday 26 July for Open Day – the stop where everything starts. Got everything you need? <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/courses/intakes/mid-year/">Apply for midyear now and get on your way in Semester 2</a>.</p> <p> <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/openday/?siid=bnr_alt%7Ccamp_mid%7Csrcnam_cs%7Csrcloc_alt%7C454"> Register for Open Day </a> </p> <h5>Your industry experience</h5> <p>Bolster your CV with real industry experience while you study through our Work Integrated Learning programs – a guaranteed part of all our bachelor degrees. This can include placements, internships or industry-linked projects. This degree includes a capstone (final year) project which could see you working with places like City of Melbourne, and more.</p> <p> <a href="/life-at-swinburne/work-integrated-learning"> Explore Work Integrated Learning </a> </p> <h5>Skills you’ll learn</h5> <ul><li> Creative problem solving </li> <li> Idea generation </li> <li> Digital prototyping </li> <li> Concept development </li> <li> Digital design skills </li> <li> Critical thinking </li> </ul> <h5>Your career opportunities</h5> <ul><li> Communication designer </li> <li> Motion designer </li> <li> Photographer </li> <li> User experience designer </li> <li> Design consultant </li> <li> Innovation lead </li> </ul> <h5>Key codes</h5> <p> CRICOS course code </p> <p> 108353M </p> <p> VTAC Code (IFP) </p> <p> 3400212573 </p> <h5> International student visa </h5> <p>International students in Australia who hold student visas are required to study full-time and on campus. Courses that are taught entirely online are only available to international students studying outside Australia or those in Australia who are not on a student visa. Online courses are not available to international students in Australia who hold a student visa.</p> <h5>Why Swinburne?</h5> <p>Top 100 for art and design</p> <p>5 stars for overall experience</p> <p>#1 in Melbourne for graduate found full-time employment 4 months after completing their degree </p> <p>#1 in Melbourne for graduate salary one year out</p> <p><a href="/life-at-swinburne/why-choose-swinburne/sources">Sources</a></p> <p> <a href="#"> Close video </a> </p> <p>Olivia''s Next Gen Story</p> <h5> Olivia''s Next Gen_ Story </h5> <p>It’s this piece of paper – a Swinburne double degree in Engineering and Business - that has prepared Olivia to start her career in the real world. Where there’s hard work, there’s also play. Olivia makes the perfect balance between her studies, and taking full advantage of the extracurricular activities Swinburne has on offer. It’s more than a piece of paper.</p> <p> <a href="https://commons.swinburne.edu.au/file/63806f98-e5db-49b8-895c-17e0cc0715c5/1/olivia_next_gen_transcript.pdf"> View transcript [PDF 171KB] </a> </p>',
