UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>Become a key player in a tech-driven world where privacy is paramount. Study a Bachelor of Business Analytics/ Bachelor of Cyber Security, and turn data into meaningful narratives. We''ll teach you to innovate and solve business, technology, and analytics problems. You''ll develop expertise in secure programming, risk management and cyber resilience, applying your skills to any business.</p> <p> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-business-analytics-bachelor-of-cyber-security/handbook"> Check the Bachelor of Business Analytics/Bachelor of Cyber Security handbook </a> </p> <p> <a href="/courses/find-a-course/download-course-guide"> Get a copy of our course guide </a> </p> <h5> Swinburne Open Day 2026 </h5> <p>Stop by our Hawthorn campus on Sunday 26 July for Open Day – the stop where everything starts. Got everything you need? <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/courses/intakes/mid-year/">Apply for midyear now and get on your way in Semester 2</a>.</p> <p> <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/openday/?siid=bnr_alt%7Ccamp_mid%7Csrcnam_cs%7Csrcloc_alt%7C454"> Register for Open Day </a> </p> <h5>Your majors</h5> <h5>Business Analysis</h5> <p>Learn how to speak and interpret both business and tech languages. Hone your strategic thinking to identify business operational challenges and how data can predict opportunities and create solutions.</p> <h5>Cyber Security</h5> <p>The cyber security industry is huge and growing quickly. Stake your career claim with our Cyber Security major.</p> <p>Learn the fundamentals of encryption systems, access control, the internet, and get into the minds of malicious hackers and cyber-criminals. Learn their tricks and how to defeat them. All with hands-on industry experience through Work Integrated Learning.</p> <h5>Your industry experience</h5> <p>Our Work Integrated Learning program bolsters your CV with real industry experience such as placements, internships and industry-linked projects. In this course, you’ll undertake six projects – one per semester – and each will build on the last.</p> <p> <a href="/life-at-swinburne/work-integrated-learning"> Explore Work Integrated Learning </a> </p> <h5>Skills you’ll learn</h5> <ul><li> Data analysis &amp; interpretation </li> <li> Strategic problem solving </li> <li> Business process modelling </li> <li> Cyber security testing/strategy </li> <li> Cyber security strategy </li> <li> Problem-solving </li> </ul> <h5>Your career opportunities</h5> <ul><li> Business analyst </li> <li> Data analyst </li> <li> Business intelligence specialist </li> <li> Information security analyst </li> <li> Security consultant </li> <li> Project manager </li> </ul> <h5>Key codes</h5> <p> CRICOS course code </p> <p> 118263H </p> <p> VTAC Code (IFP) </p> <p> 3400213063 </p> <h5> International student visa </h5> <p>International students in Australia who hold student visas are required to study full-time and on campus. Courses that are taught entirely online are only available to international students studying outside Australia or those in Australia who are not on a student visa. Online courses are not available to international students in Australia who hold a student visa.</p> <h5>Professional accreditations</h5> <ul><li> <a href="https://www.acs.org.au"> <h5> Australian Computer Society </h5> </a> </li> </ul> <h5>Why Swinburne?</h5> <p>Top 5% of the world’s higher education business schools</p> <p>#1 in Melbourne for student support</p> <p>#1 in Victoria for Graduate Employability and Salary</p> QILT Graduate Outcomes Survey (GOS) 2024 <p>#1 in Australia for Computer Science and Engineering</p> <p>ARWU Global Ranking of Academic Subjects 2025</p> <p><a href="/life-at-swinburne/why-choose-swinburne/sources">Sources</a></p>',
