UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>Innovation is the driving force behind our technolgically-charged world. Study the unique combination of Computer Science / Bachelor of Applied Innovation to stay ahead of the curve. Develop expertise in software development and learn contemporary approaches to the analysis, design and implementation of large-scale systems. Apply human-centered design and innovation principles to make strategic and creative decisions.</p> <p> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-computer-science-bachelor-of-applied-innovation/handbook"> View Bachelor of Computer Science / Bachelor of Applied Innovation course handbook </a> </p> <p> <a href="/courses/find-a-course/download-course-guide"> Get a copy of our course guide </a> </p> <h5> Swinburne Open Day 2026 </h5> <p>Stop by our Hawthorn campus on Sunday 26 July for Open Day – the stop where everything starts. Got everything you need? <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/courses/intakes/mid-year/">Apply for midyear now and get on your way in Semester 2</a>.</p> <p> <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/openday/?siid=bnr_alt%7Ccamp_mid%7Csrcnam_cs%7Csrcloc_alt%7C454"> Register for Open Day </a> </p> <h5>Your industry experience</h5> <p>Bolster your CV with real industry experience while you study through our Work Integrated Learning programs – a guaranteed part of all our bachelor degrees. This can include placements, internships or industry-linked projects.</p> <p> <a href="/life-at-swinburne/work-integrated-learning"> Explore Work Integrated Learning </a> </p> <h5>Skills you’ll learn</h5> <ul><li> Critical thinking </li> <li> Creative problem-solving </li> <li> Adaptability </li> <li> Computer software development </li> <li> Machine learning application </li> <li> Problem solving </li> </ul> <h5>Your career opportunities</h5> <ul><li> Systems developer </li> <li> Project manager </li> <li> Innovation analyst </li> <li> Strategic designer </li> <li> Innovation consultant </li> <li> Innovation lead </li> </ul> <h5>Key codes</h5> <p> CRICOS course code </p> <p> 108352A </p> <p> VTAC Code (IFP) </p> <p> 3400212553 </p> <h5> International student visa </h5> <p>International students in Australia who hold student visas are required to study full-time and on campus. Courses that are taught entirely online are only available to international students studying outside Australia or those in Australia who are not on a student visa. Online courses are not available to international students in Australia who hold a student visa.</p> <h5>Professional accreditations</h5> <ul></ul> <h5>Why Swinburne?</h5> <p>#1 in Australia for Computer Science and Engineering</p> <p>ARWU Global Ranking of Academic Subjects 2025</p> <p>#1 in Victoria for Graduate Employability and Salary</p> QILT Graduate Outcomes Survey (GOS) 2024 <p>#6 in Australia for Artificial Intelligence</p> US News: Best Global Universities <p>Top 150 Best Global Universities</p> <p>US News: Best Global University Rankings 2025-2026</p> <p><a href="/life-at-swinburne/why-choose-swinburne/sources">Sources</a></p> <p> <a href="#"> Close video </a> </p> <p>Olivia''s Next Gen Story</p> <h5> Olivia''s Next Gen_ Story </h5> <p>It’s this piece of paper – a Swinburne double degree in Engineering and Business - that has prepared Olivia to start her career in the real world. Where there’s hard work, there’s also play. Olivia makes the perfect balance between her studies, and taking full advantage of the extracurricular activities Swinburne has on offer. It’s more than a piece of paper.</p> <p> <a href="https://commons.swinburne.edu.au/file/63806f98-e5db-49b8-895c-17e0cc0715c5/1/olivia_next_gen_transcript.pdf"> View transcript [PDF 171KB] </a> </p>',
