UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>Innovation meets media and communication in this next-gen double degree. Dive into diversity. Investigate the influence of social networking data, ownership and privacy, automated media, the digital economy, and more in our Bachelor of Media and Communication / Bachelor of Applied Innovation. Pair it with hackathons, industry projects and innovation sprints. Emerge ready to drive positive change.</p> <p> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-media-and-communication-bachelor-of-applied-innovation/handbook"> View Bachelor of Media and Communication / Bachelor of Applied Innovation course handbook </a> </p> <p> <a href="/courses/find-a-course/download-course-guide"> Get a copy of our course guide </a> </p> <h5> Swinburne Open Day 2026 </h5> <p>Stop by our Hawthorn campus on Sunday 26 July for Open Day – the stop where everything starts. Got everything you need? <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/courses/intakes/mid-year/">Apply for midyear now and get on your way in Semester 2</a>.</p> <p> <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/openday/?siid=bnr_alt%7Ccamp_mid%7Csrcnam_cs%7Csrcloc_alt%7C454"> Register for Open Day </a> </p> <h5>Your industry experience</h5> <p>Bolster your CV with real industry experience while you study through our Work Integrated Learning programs – a guaranteed part of all our bachelor degrees. This can include placements, internships or industry-linked projects.</p> <p> <a href="/life-at-swinburne/work-integrated-learning"> Explore Work Integrated Learning </a> </p> <h5>Skills you’ll learn</h5> <ul><li> Media content creation </li> <li> Communicating for influence and impact </li> <li> Critical and analytical thinking </li> <li> Creative problem-solving </li> <li> Adaptability </li> <li> Collaboration </li> </ul> <h5>Your career opportunities</h5> <ul><li> Communications strategist </li> <li> Marketing communications specialist </li> <li> Content marketing manager </li> <li> Innovation consultant </li> <li> Strategic designer </li> <li> Creative producer </li> </ul> <h5>Key codes</h5> <p> CRICOS course code </p> <p> 108358F </p> <p> VTAC Code (IFP) </p> <p> 3400212613 </p> <h5> International student visa </h5> <p>International students in Australia who hold student visas are required to study full-time and on campus. Courses that are taught entirely online are only available to international students studying outside Australia or those in Australia who are not on a student visa. Online courses are not available to international students in Australia who hold a student visa.</p> <h5>Professional accreditations</h5> <ul><li> <a href="https://www.mediafederation.org.au/"> <h5> Media Federation of Australia (MFA) </h5> </a> </li> <li> <a href="https://www.cpra.org.au/"> <h5> Communication Public Relations Australia (CPRA) </h5> </a> </li> </ul> <h5>Why Swinburne?</h5> <p>Top 200 for communication</p> <p>#1 in Melbourne for overall experience</p> <p>Advertising students win 2022 Annual Advertising Capstone Challenge (ACC)</p> <p><a href="/life-at-swinburne/why-choose-swinburne/sources">Sources</a></p>',
