UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>Ever wondered if technology could enable a crime-free society? Learn about the causes of crime and how police, courts, corrections systems and victim support services respond. Plus, gain a strong innovation mindset through multidisciplinary hackathons and industry projects. Hone your leadership potential, sharpen your analytical and strategic thinking and embrace a deeper level of human understanding.</p> <p> <a href="/course/undergraduate/bachelor-of-criminal-justice-and-criminology-bachelor-of-applied-innovation/handbook"> View Bachelor of Criminal Justice and Criminology / Bachelor of Applied Innovation course handbook </a> </p> <p> <a href="/courses/find-a-course/download-course-guide"> Get a copy of our course guide </a> </p> <h5> Swinburne Open Day 2026 </h5> <p>Stop by our Hawthorn campus on Sunday 26 July for Open Day – the stop where everything starts. Got everything you need? <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/courses/intakes/mid-year/">Apply for midyear now and get on your way in Semester 2</a>.</p> <p> <a href="https://www.swinburne.edu.au/openday/?siid=bnr_alt%7Ccamp_mid%7Csrcnam_cs%7Csrcloc_alt%7C454"> Register for Open Day </a> </p> <h5>Your industry experience</h5> <p>Bolster your CV with real industry experience while you study through our Work Integrated Learning programs – a guaranteed part of all our bachelor degrees. This can include placements, internships or industry-linked projects.</p> <p> <a href="/life-at-swinburne/work-integrated-learning"> Explore Work Integrated Learning </a> </p> <h5>Skills you’ll learn</h5> <ul><li> Effective communication </li> <li> Cultural awareness </li> <li> Criminal justice and criminology research </li> <li> Critical thinking </li> <li> Adaptability </li> <li> Creative problem-solving </li> </ul> <h5>Your career opportunities</h5> <ul><li> Victim support worker </li> <li> Government policy writer </li> <li> Law enforcement officer </li> <li> Innovation analyst </li> <li> Human-centred researcher </li> <li> Transformation lead </li> </ul> <h5>Key codes</h5> <p> CRICOS course code </p> <p> 108351B </p> <p> VTAC Code (IFP) </p> <p> 3400212563 </p> <h5> International student visa </h5> <p>International students in Australia who hold student visas are required to study full-time and on campus. Courses that are taught entirely online are only available to international students studying outside Australia or those in Australia who are not on a student visa. Online courses are not available to international students in Australia who hold a student visa.</p> <h5>Why Swinburne?</h5> <p>Top 400 for arts and humanities</p> <p>5 stars for overall experience</p> <p>5 stars for teaching quality</p> <p>#1 in Melbourne for graduate salary</p> <p><a href="/life-at-swinburne/why-choose-swinburne/sources">Sources</a></p> <p> <a href="#"> Close video </a> </p> <p>Olivia''s Next Gen Story</p> <h5> Olivia''s Next Gen_ Story </h5> <p>It’s this piece of paper – a Swinburne double degree in Engineering and Business - that has prepared Olivia to start her career in the real world. Where there’s hard work, there’s also play. Olivia makes the perfect balance between her studies, and taking full advantage of the extracurricular activities Swinburne has on offer. It’s more than a piece of paper.</p> <p> <a href="https://commons.swinburne.edu.au/file/63806f98-e5db-49b8-895c-17e0cc0715c5/1/olivia_next_gen_transcript.pdf"> View transcript [PDF 171KB] </a> </p>',
